 "paragraphs": [
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Twin Delayed DDPG (TD3)",
   "id": "s0-title",
   "kind": "section_title",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 0
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "A robot-arm learner that scores its turning forces with two netw",
   "id": "s0-p1",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 0
  },
  {
   "domId": "td3-problem",
   "fp": "1 Why the scoring network rates moves too high",
   "id": "s1-title",
   "kind": "section_title",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Deep Deterministic Policy Gradient (DDPG) trains one network, th",
   "id": "s1-p1",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "The agent is the learner that picks the moves. (RL Basics) A sta",
   "id": "s1-p2",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 2,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Twin Delayed DDPG (TD3) is DDPG with three changes that reduce t",
   "id": "s1-p3",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 3,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "The running example is the Reacher task from Unity ML-Agents, a ",
   "id": "s1-p4",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 4,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": "fig-td3-reacher",
   "fp": "Figure 1. The Reacher arm, with two joints, four torques and a m",
   "id": "s1-f1",
   "kind": "figure",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "The arm in Figure 1 stands near a dashed goal circle that moves.",
   "id": "s1-p5",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 5,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "The return is all the reward still to come, with later rewards c",
   "id": "s1-p6",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 6,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "The deterministic actor is a network with weights that outputs o",
   "id": "s1-p7",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 7,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "1.1 The actor follows scores that were never real",
   "id": "s1-h1",
   "kind": "subhead",
   "ordinal": 1,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Overestimation",
   "id": "s1-p8",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 8,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "What. Overestimation means the values rise above the return the ",
   "id": "s1-p9",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 9,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "How. The actor update follows the gradient up, so it moves towar",
   "id": "s1-p10",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 10,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Why. The actor follows scores that were never real, and the crit",
   "id": "s1-p11",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 11,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": "fig-td3-overest",
   "fp": "Figure 2. A sketch: the critic's estimate sits above the true va",
   "id": "s1-f2",
   "kind": "figure",
   "ordinal": 2,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "The critic's estimate sits above the true value over time while ",
   "id": "s1-p12",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 12,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "1.2 Why Double DQN's fix does not carry over to DDPG",
   "id": "s1-h2",
   "kind": "subhead",
   "ordinal": 2,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "The slow copy",
   "id": "s1-p13",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 13,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "What. The critic learns by being pulled toward a target, the num",
   "id": "s1-p14",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 14,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "How. The live network learns while the slow copy stands almost s",
   "id": "s1-p15",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 15,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Why. The critic's scores move toward a target that barely moves ",
   "id": "s1-p16",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 16,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "The target is the step's reward plus its own score for what come",
   "id": "s1-p17",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 17,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "In the value methods, which learn by scoring moves, the critic i",
   "id": "s1-p18",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 18,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "In DDPG both the actor and the critic have a slow copy, marked b",
   "id": "s1-p19",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 19,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "For value methods, overestimation already has a known fix. Doubl",
   "id": "s1-p20",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 20,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "In DDPG the same trick would let the live actor pick the next to",
   "id": "s1-p21",
   "kind": "prose",
   "ordinal": 21,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "1.3 Errors grow through the target",
   "id": "s1-h3",
   "kind": "subhead",
   "ordinal": 3,
   "section": 1
  },
  {
   "domId": null,
   "fp": "Bootstrapping: errors carry forward",
